.TH RUSTGIS-GRASS-SETUP 1 "2026-11-03" "rustgis-grass-plugin 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustgis\-grass\-setup \- set up the GRASS GIS plugin for RustGIS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustgis\-grass\-setup
.RI [ \-\-remove ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates the plugin's manifest from the GRASS GIS installed on this machine
and registers the plugin with RustGIS, for the user who runs the command.
.PP
The manifest is not shipped in the package: a module's parameter labels are
part of GRASS's own documentation, which is GPL\-2.0\-or\-later. The plugin's
code is therefore copied out of
.I /usr/share/rustgis\-grass\-plugin
into
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/rustgis\-grass\-plugin ,
where the manifest is generated by reading
.B <module> \-\-interface\-description
from the installation found here.
.PP
Run it again after upgrading GRASS or this package, so the forms match the
modules.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-remove
Unregister the plugin from RustGIS and delete the per\-user folder.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTGIS_GRASS
The GRASS launcher to use, when it is not on the
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Where the per\-user folder is made. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.SH EXIT STATUS
Non\-zero when python3, rustgis\-cli or GRASS is missing, or when the manifest
cannot be generated.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/rustgis\-grass\-plugin
The plugin's code, as the package installs it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/rustgis\-grass\-plugin
The copy RustGIS runs, with the generated manifest.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grass (1)
.PP
https://github.com/YannChemin/rustgis\-grass\-plugin
